Phase 1: Project Adapter loading and enforceable execution mode

The mode ladder is now real rather than advisory. A declaration is cross-checked
against the project's declared high-risk paths and escalated when it should be,
which is the outline's 5/6 gate: semantic impact decides, file count never does.

- lib/project-state.js  loads <root>/.dsh/gac/project.json, validates it through
                        lib/project.js, and holds the per-session mode decision.
                        The caching contract is the interesting part and is
                        tested directly: absence IS cached, an INVALID adapter is
                        NOT (it is a transient authoring mistake the user is
                        fixing right now), and absence is not an error at all.
- lib/tool-project.js   gac_project: inspect the adapter, or declare a mode. Its
                        description carries the mode ladder with each level's
                        consequence rather than its name, because "standard_task"
                        means nothing on its own.
- .dsh/gac/project.json this repository's own adapter, so the plugin governs
                        itself: lib/write-scope.js, lib/plugin.js and the other
                        enforcement primitives are declared high-risk.

Verified against the real adapter: a direct_edit targeting lib/write-scope.js
escalates to high_risk_task with the declared mode preserved alongside the
resolved one, so both the claim and the outcome remain auditable.

Fixed while testing: tool-project dereferenced a null adapter when a session had
no project root, throwing a TypeError at the model instead of a sentence it could
act on. The root is now checked before inspecting, and the rootless path never
reaches the adapter at all.

Also fixed: project-state's path join mixed separators (C:\a + .dsh/gac/x.json),
producing a path that reads fine in a message and that readFileSync rejects.
Paths are now reported /-separated on every platform, matching the convention
write-scope normalises to, and converted to native form only at the filesystem
call.

184 tests pass. HMR reloaded the plugin with both tools registered
(["gac_project","gac_scope"]) without a restart.
